# Git branches

Work in the **current checkout**. Do **not** switch branches, checkout `main`, or `git stash` unless the user explicitly asks.

The app on screen is the source of truth. Edits must land in these files so the running dev server updates live.

## Do not

- `git checkout main`
- `git checkout -b …` for a new feature
- `git stash` (including `stash push -u`) to “get a clean tree”

Those hide uncommitted work and make the site jump back to an old version.

## When the user asks to commit / PR / ship

Then follow **ship-feature-to-main**: commit on the **current** branch, push that branch, open a PR into `main` if they asked.

If they later want a named feature branch, they will say so. Until then, keep everything on whatever branch is already checked out.
